        <definition>dht20_error_t DHT20::readTempAndHumidity</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>readTempAndHumidity</name>
        <qualifiedname>DHT20::readTempAndHumidity</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Reads temperature and humidity data from the <ref refid="class_d_h_t20" kindref="compound">DHT20</ref> sensor. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function attempts to read temperature and humidity data from the <ref refid="class_d_h_t20" kindref="compound">DHT20</ref> sensor. It retries the operation multiple times if the sensor is not ready or data is not available. The raw sensor values are then converted to floating-point temperature and humidity values.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">None</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>Ensure that the sensor is correctly connected and that I2C communication is functioning. This function may block for short periods while waiting for the sensor to be ready and for data to be available.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>DHT20_OK</computeroutput>: Success</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>DHT20_TIMEOUT</computeroutput>: Timeout, the sensor is not ready or data is not available after multiple attempts. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
