        <definition>dht20_error_t DHT20::readTargetData</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint32_t *data)</argsstring>
        <name>readTargetData</name>
        <qualifiedname>DHT20::readTargetData</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t *</type>
          <declname>data</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Reads temperature and humidity data from the <ref refid="class_d_h_t20" kindref="compound">DHT20</ref> sensor. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function reads a 6-byte buffer from the <ref refid="class_d_h_t20" kindref="compound">DHT20</ref> sensor, where the first byte is the status register, and the remaining 5 bytes contain temperature and humidity data. It processes these bytes to extract the humidity and temperature values.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">None</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to a buffer where the temperature and humidity data will be stored.<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>data[HUMIDITY_INDEX]</computeroutput> will hold the processed humidity data.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>data[TEMPERATURE_INDEX]</computeroutput> will hold the processed temperature data.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>Ensure that the sensor is properly connected and that the I2C communication is functioning. The function waits for 80 milliseconds for the measurement to complete, which might block other operations during this time.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>DHT20_OK</computeroutput>: Success</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>DHT20_ERR_I2C_WRITE</computeroutput>: Error writing to the I2C bus</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>DHT20_ERR_I2C_READ</computeroutput>: Error reading from the I2C bus</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>DHT20_ERR</computeroutput>: Sensor is still busy or not ready </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
